target/
*.pdb

# Local-only EVIDENCE and harness scratch. Same policy as the docs below — these are captures and
# working files, not code: they are regenerated by running the harness, several are tens of megabytes
# of PNG, and a remote full of screenshots is a remote nobody can clone. Keep producing them locally;
# they just never travel.
/editor-shell/e2e/.shots-*/
/editor-shell/evidence/
# NOT ignored, deliberately: `editor-shell/e2e/baselines/` and `editor-shell/e2e/fixtures/`. Those are
# authored GOLDEN inputs, not run output — `compare-renders.ps1` says outright that it never updates a
# baseline, which only means anything if the baseline travels with the code. A golden image that exists
# on one machine is not a gate.
/picking-evidence/
/.uxtest/
# Two orphaned cargo target directories that the `target/` rule above does not match by name —
# 26.8 GB and 926 MB respectively when this was written.
/.codex-pipe-target/
/target-scene-glb-agent/
# Vite writes a transient bundled copy of a TypeScript config beside the config it loaded, named
# `<config>.timestamp-<ms>-<hash>.mjs`, and deletes it on a clean exit. A killed or timed-out build
# leaves it behind, so four had accumulated as untracked files — the same ambient-noise problem as
# `/__probe` above, and worse, because each one is a plausible-looking `.mjs` sitting next to real
# scripts. They are build output; they never travel.
*.timestamp-*.mjs
# Per-machine agent permission grants. The `.local.json` suffix is the convention's own statement that
# this belongs to one workstation — it records which commands a human approved HERE, which is neither
# code nor a decision anyone else can act on. Same local-only rule as the docs below.
/.claude/settings.local.json
# The zero-byte file the session harness drops at the mount root to prove the mount is writable.
# It reappears every session; without this it shows up as an untracked file in every `git status`,
# which is exactly the ambient noise that trains a reader to stop looking at the list.
/__probe
# One-off scratch: a layout probe binary + its source, and two extraction dumps.
/check_layout
/check_layout.rs
/scratch_recs.txt
/usd_glossary_extract.txt
# Brand source art (large binaries, and IP that follows the same local-only rule as the docs).
/Logo and Branding/

# Documentation is local-only, private IP (orchestrator policy; prompt 29 "repo-take-docs-private").
# The remote carries CODE only — the vision, roadmap, ADRs, progress logs, prompts and READMEs stay
# local and un-pushed by design. Do NOT re-add a doc to the remote or "fix" this ignore.
*.md
/prompts/
/progress/
/decisions/
/docs/

# Python bytecode from the repo tools (gpu-contract-audit)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
